Subject: [PATCH] Invite only through every door: the connector sign-in asks
 the gate (5419)

The connector's sign-in (/oauth/authorize, used by ChatGPT and Claude)
admitted any number in "UserPhone", the legacy Ally accounts among them,
with no invitation. It never asked the login gate the app's own sign-in
asks, and a thread made through the connector then made the account
"belong to Netai", so the app's gate opened for it too.

Both connector steps (send-code and verify) now take the account only when
loginGateVerdict would admit it, the same verdict completeLogin applies.
A refused number gets the page's existing "not registered" line; no new
text.

